---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Tracey and the art of quilling — handmade paper art from Australia.">

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

        <!-- About Tracey -->
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-semibold text-ink">About Tracey</h1>
        <!-- TODO: Tracey to replace this placeholder with her own words -->
        <p class="mt-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Tracey is a self-taught quilling artist based in Australia. What started as a
          creative hobby quickly grew into a passion for intricate paper art. Today she
          works from her home studio, creating everything from small greeting cards to
          large framed statement pieces and personalised commissions.
        </p>
        <!-- TODO: Add photo of Tracey / studio here -->
        <div class="mt-8 aspect-[4/3] rounded-lg bg-border/30 flex items-center justify-center">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">Photo placeholder — Tracey / studio</p>
        </div>

        <!-- About quilling -->
        <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-ink">What is quilling?</h2>
        <!-- TODO: Tracey to review and personalise -->
        <p class="mt-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Quilling is the art of rolling, shaping and gluing thin strips of paper into
          decorative designs. It dates back centuries — historically used to decorate
          religious objects and book covers — but has evolved into a modern craft with
          endless creative possibilities.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Each shape is formed by hand: tight coils, loose scrolls, teardrops, marquise
          shapes, and more. These individual elements are then arranged and layered to
          create the finished artwork. The result is a textured, three-dimensional piece
          that catches the light beautifully.
        </p>

        <!-- Studio + materials -->
        <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif font-semibold text-ink">Studio &amp; materials</h2>
        <!-- TODO: Tracey to add details about her materials and workspace -->
        <p class="mt-6 text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Tracey uses high-quality quilling paper strips in a wide range of colours and
          widths, along with archival-safe adhesives to ensure each piece lasts. Framed
          works are mounted in shadow-box frames that protect the dimensional paper
          elements while allowing the depth and texture to be fully appreciated.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
